  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Say name",
   "texto": [
    "**Benim adım Anna** means «My name is Anna.»; in conversation, **Adım Anna** is usually enough.",
    "**Ben Anna'yım** («soy Anna») adds a person's termination to the name. After a name of its own, the suffix is separated with an apothrome: **Anna'yım**.",
    "**Memnun oldum** means «Nice to meet you.»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask the name",
   "texto": [
    "**Adın ne?** = what's your name? (informal). **Adınız ne?** is the courteous or plural form.",
    "**Ne?** means «What?». In Turkish, many questions of yes / no use the separate particle **mi/mı/mu/mü**; in this lesson it appears in **Türk müsün?** («Are you Turkish?»)."
   ]
  },
